notes: >-
  run_scm() call sites already used named args, so the arg-order change needed
  no edits. The build_schedule() site in R/community_plant.R relied on
  attr(p_new, "offspring_production"); migrated to read scm$parameters and
  scm$offspring_production off the SCM object.

  2026-08-13: bumped the recorded baseline from 2.0.0.9001 to the installed
  2.0.0.9002 and started a non_breaking_changes section. FF16 gains a_f4 and
  a_f5, a reproductive-allocation reaction norm on canopy openness; both default
  to 0.0 and reproduce the existing FF16 behaviour exactly, so nothing in
  regnans changes.

  2026-10-07: pinned plant_ref to the develop commit the suite was run against
  (traitecoevo/regnans#32) rather than the moving branch name. Neither new
  breaking change needed an edit here. unknown-trait-error: regnans passes only
  its trait-matrix columns to generate_strategy(), and the plant tests use real
  FF16 parameters (lma, hmat). It does retract the 2026-08-13 claim that any
  trait-matrix column reaches pars: a_f4 and a_f5 can be evolved here only once
  the FF16 change that adds them is on develop (it is not at 6cc5da4), and until
  then naming one is an error rather than a silent no-op. tf24-leaf-renames:
  regnans names no TF24 parameter; harness_plant(model = "TF24") is metadata
  only. The odelia pin (815a54f) is the one plant pins, as pak requires.

  2026-10-10: plant#648. Dropping the use_ode_times argument was not enough on
  its own, because run_scm() now replays any schedule p carries.
  The equilibrium runner fed each refinement's p (which now records ode_times
  and ode_step_sizes) back into the next iteration, so each refinement replayed
  the previous birth rate's steps. The runner now clears both before refining,
  so it integrates freely as before. The resident run for mutant fitness
  replayed ode_times alone, which lets the controller sub-step. That run no
  longer matched the equilibrium run (resident fitness -0.016, not 0), so
  model_support now carries node_schedule_ode_step_sizes alongside
  node_schedule_ode_times. community_add() clears both. The empty-community
  mutant run clears both to integrate freely (was use_ode_times = 0).
  save_RK45_cache was dropped from the resident control.

  2026-10-14: plant#657, #661, #662, #676 and #658, which make an FF16
  stand's census and fitness differentiable (plant#650 E1-E4). No edit was
  needed: regnans builds invader parameters from the resident's own, which
  carry no initial state, and sets no patch_type. All three plant smoke files
  passed against bd09645d before any other change. The gradients run on the
  birth-date coordinate only, so harness_plant() moves to it in the same PR.

  2026-11-09: 33 plant commits, bd09645d..a7729146. Two renames were
  mechanical (node-density-coordinate, keep-states). The third was not named
  as breaking for FF16 in plant's NEWS but broke every plant test here: a
  refining run records four schedule fields into its parameters, and the
  runner cleared two, so the next iteration handed plant soil records without
  step sizes, which its SCM constructor refuses. The four now travel as one
  (plant_clear_ode_schedule(); model_support, the discretisation and
  community_add() carry or clear all four). Every pinned number in the plant
  smoke files held at its tolerance under Hairer stepping. scripts/gps/optim.Rmd
  (not run by the suite) had the two plant#648 mappings applied, found by the
  PR's independent review.

  2026-11-10: plant#731 (fieldtrial PR A with PR B folded in). Trade-offs now
  travel on the Parameters object (p$hyperpar); the bare scm_base_parameters()
  attaches none and the old hyperpar names are gone. One edit:
  plant_default_assembly_pars() builds on default_parameters(model, quiet =
  TRUE), which attaches plant's frozen testing trade-offs, the same functions
  the assembly ran under before. Every other call site already went through
  plant::param_hyperpar(p), which now reads the carried function, so
  community_plant.R needed nothing else. The pin names the PR head; repoint it
  to the develop commit of the squash merge when bumping next.
